{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1528179-communication-and-fetters","id":1528179,"title":"Communication and Fetters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-07T15:18:31-08:00","id":1528179,"title":"Communication and Fetters","content":"I am posting this question here on behalf of another in hopes of finding an answer for them. I have done a copy-pasta of their question, and I hope to do the same with a great response for them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm currently preparing my first game of Wraith, set in 1840 England.<br /> <br /> I've got a general plot idea that sends my players from orderly York to a small hamlet in countryside, then to the cramped slums of Manchester.<br /> <br /> Now I'm running into two problems:<br /> 1) how do wraiths communicate over longer distances? Unlike vampires they can't just send a letter, right? How would word of something happening in one place reach wraiths in another? Are there wraith postmen?<br /> <br /> 2) wraiths are, well, fettered to their fetters, and unless said Fetters have become relics somehow, they can't really take them with them.<br /> <br /> So what happens, when a Wraith has to travel? How does the Hierarchy station legionaires in places where their Fetters are not?<br /> <br /> For instance, I'm planning to have a few legionaires put under the regent of the small hamlet mentioned above. But none of them are from that village. How would that normally work?<br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T21:17:35-08:00","id":1528201,"title":"","content":"Here are my answers.<br /> <br /> 1) There are enough wraiths that there is actually a functional government, albeit one that is more reminiscent of the Classical empires than modern day governments. There are probably wraiths skilled in Argos that are willing to deliver letters or messages and the like. Certainly Necropoli need to send reports to Stygia. There might also be artifacts or relics that might allow communication over long distances. I imagine most news is reported in the Citadel by the equivalent of cryers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xH0kO5qcPf8\" data-code=\"xH0kO5qcPf8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xH0kO5qcPf8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 2) Wraiths are not limited to locations that their fetters are at. Fetters simply allow wraiths to permanently stay in the Shadowlands as a whole. Simply because their fetters are in Scotland does not mean they cannot be in Germany, India, or Brazil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T23:38:23-08:00","id":1528202,"title":"","content":"Fetters are fetters not because wraiths are <i>physically</i> bound to them, but because they're <i>metaphysically/psychologically</i> bound to them - they're the things that anchor them to the Shadowlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T02:59:40-08:00","id":1528251,"title":"","content":"I was convinced there was a Lifeweb art that enables communication between two Wraiths, but turns out that Monitors have plenty of arts that are <i>adjacent </i>to that. In Great War there is a level 1 variant that allows a Monitor to link two Wraiths with a pseudo-Fetter, but the benefits are more for anchoring them in the Shadowlands. Spectres with Hive-Mind can communicate telepathically with each other, though.<br /> <br /> But establishing a communication link <i>feels </i>like something Monitors should be able to do. I would probably allow this as an alternative level 1 art. On the other hand, having Harbingers deliver letters or Chanteurs do the bardic news thing is a nice setting detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T03:14:04-08:00","id":1528253,"title":"","content":"Maybe make it a recent development thing, essentially turning Lifeweb into the Underworld equivalent of the Internet. Basically a 21sy century innovation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T11:25:21-08:00","id":1528378,"title":"","content":"Another possibility is that Stygia may have assembled enough relics to allow for some kind of long distance communication. If they have functioning relic trains and airplanes, then they could have functioning radio towers, radios, telegraphs, etc. A lot of it would probably be military equipment destroyed in war, but there could also be some destroyed in natural disasters or fires. Instead of electricity, it would have to be powered by Pathos.<br /> <br /> The Hierarchy is probably the only faction organized enough to establish and maintain such a system, but it would still be possible for the occasional Renegade &quot;pirate radio station&quot; to exist.<br /> <br /> Instead of a modern day internet, I imagine it would be more primitive and infrequently used - more like early twentieth century technology level at best than anything post-WWII. It could be the Shadowlands only capable of communicating with somewhere else in the Shadowlands, with communications between Stygia/Tempest and Shadowlands done only with difficulty and rarity, or not at all.<br /> <br /> There's a trope of people receiving ghostly radio signals so it fits with folklore.<br /> <br /> If I was going to use that in a chronicle, I would probably limit it to a jury-rigged telegraph/teletype system (accommodating all sorts of random hardware) for official Hierarchy use plus extremely rare ghost radio stations. There might not even be even one such radio station in many Necropolis, and no more than one in any Necropolis. And only those with relic radios could be able to listen to it. All such radio stations would be strictly controlled by the Hierarchy and mostly used for official communications and approved entertainment. Though the occasional Renegade (or even Heretic) pirate radio would exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T11:08:51-08:00","id":1528424,"title":"","content":"Hm, communication devices are fairly good candidates for becoming Relics. Especially the closer you get to modern times, there is a lot of emotion connected to phones. For an early 20th century setting, two Citadels having a rare Relic telegraph line between them wouldn't be totally out of the question.<br /> In modern times Artificers can use Skinland infrastructure to make communication easy with a bit of coordination. The New Arts for Inhabit are clearly from the computer era, but I could see Artificers experiment with something like the telegraph and radio relatively early - ie that could still work for the latter half of the 19th century. 1840 is really early, though.<br /> <br /> I vaguely remember a weather station in one of the book's fluff that uses a radio transmitter to broadcast maelstrom warnings, but I forget which one. I love the idea of Shadowlands radio becoming ghost signals in the Skinlands though, or Wraiths assembling something like a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foxhole_radio\" target=\"_blank\">foxhole radio</a> from bits and bobs to pick up the signal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T03:03:07-08:00","id":1528705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1528179-communication-and-fetters?p=1528424#post1528424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I love the idea of Shadowlands radio becoming ghost signals in the Skinlands though</div> </div> </div> </div>Advocates of Radio Voice Phenomenon (RVP) claim they are able to use radio equipment in order to communicate with ghosts and spirits<br /> In order to hear Radio Voice Phenomenon, you\u2019ll need to have access to a Spirit Box and be in a potentially haunted space.<br /> Spirit Boxes (also known as Ghost Boxes) scan through the normal frequency ranges used by broadcasters to transmit radio programs on various stations or frequencies, from both the AM (535 to 1064 KHz) or FM (88 to 108 MHz) radio spectrum. <br /> Pirate Wraith radio stations despite the Dictum Mortuum are a fun idea<br /> Trukcer wraits tuning in the conversations and so on... old sailors want to save others from Davy Jones locker and trying to warn them via radio, to watch out or scare away...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1528179-communication-and-fetters?p=1528424#post1528424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hm, communication devices are fairly good candidates for becoming Relics. Especially the closer you get to modern times, there is a lot of emotion connected to phones</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally see those old antique radios from the '40s or even earlyier becoming relics, people have a real connection and attachment with those<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T17:01:50-08:00","id":1528765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1528179-communication-and-fetters?p=1528705#post1528705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to hear Radio Voice Phenomenon, you\u2019ll need to have access to a Spirit Box and be in a potentially haunted space.<br /> Spirit Boxes (also known as Ghost Boxes) scan through the normal frequency ranges used by broadcasters to transmit radio programs on various stations or frequencies, from both the AM (535 to 1064 KHz) or FM (88 to 108 MHz) radio spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not familiar with the term, but it sounds like radio voice phenomenon is the same as electronic voice phenomenon (EVP) which does not require the voices being heard to come from the kind of wraith radio systems we're talking about. They just pick up the &quot;ordinary&quot; voices of ghosts in the area (verbal communication). Now that doesn't mean for our purposes that such ghost boxes can't pick up these wraithly relic communication systems as well. But when I'm talking about people listening to ghostly radio signals, I just mean ordinary radios (can be things like ham radio as opposed to commercial radio) and the like somehow receiving these signals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1528179-communication-and-fetters?p=1528705#post1528705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trukcer wraits tuning in the conversations and so on... old sailors want to save others from Davy Jones locker and trying to warn them via radio, to watch out or scare away...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more like what I mean. It might be wraiths directly broadcasting to the Quick on purpose for some reason. But I would likely most often have it just be inadvertent receptions that people usually attribute to glitches, real pirate radio, number stations, signal hijacking, and the like. The vast majority of the time, nobody would even guess whatever weird things they hear might be from beyond the Shroud. Or something that while the communication sounds like it might be something across the Shroud, there's still plenty of room for skeptics to attribute it to pranks.<br /> <br /> If a wraithly media signal to the Quick was done on purpose, I'd probably do something similar to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@LOCAL58TV/videos\" target=\"_blank\">Kris Straub's Local58</a>.<br /> <br /> There should be some requirements like a low Shroud rating before such things can happen, and it's probably quite rare when all conditions are met. So it's not something you can plan for (unless the ST wants it as part of a plot, perhaps some variant of Fatalism can help people anticipate the best times and places to do it).<br /> <br /> Of course, the use of Inhabit can be a source of these stories as well. But that doesn't mean there can't be something else that produces such phenomenon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1528179-communication-and-fetters?p=1528705#post1528705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can totally see those old antique radios from the '40s or even earlyier becoming relics, people have a real connection and attachment with those</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there could be a wide variety of things that might cross over as relics. But they wouldn't be consistently coming over, and technology always changes. Which is why any system would have to be jury rigged and based on the lowest common denominator. It doesn't matter if a smartphone or other modern equipment crosses over if the main network medium is still something like the telegraph or early radio.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}